coin.py, realtime_price_provider.py, live_coinapi_wsds.py, live_coinapi_v1.py). (2) Run the closure scanner to confirm transitive local dependencies are present in the baseline; copy any uncovered helpers (e.g., utils, services, telegram_alerts, config_accounts) before declaring closure complete or classify them MISSING_IN_LEGACY_BASELINE with a written reason. (3) Read copied_baseline_manifest.json and CITE the SHA256 of every baseline file you actually relied on inside the LEGACY_BASELINE_ANALYSIS.md and the legacy_behavior_mapping.json (Codex review fails if SHAs are absent or don't match). (4) Produce both baseline files BEFORE writing v2/backend/app/cli/v2_market_ingestor.py. The analysis must list legacy_source_paths, legacy_functions_preserved, legacy_inputs, legacy_outputs, legacy_redis_keys (read-only references only; the V2 worker must NEVER write old Redis keys \u2014 V2 writes only v2:* namespaced streams), legacy_config_dependencies, legacy_edge_cases (rate-limit backoff, reconnect/retry, market hours, CoinAPI fallback policy), legacy_failure_modes, legacy_tests_or_expected_behavior, V2_mapping, intentional_changes, removed/deprecated behavior with reason. (5) Build v2_market_ingestor.py with the data-source priority from the startup script's data-source table (OHLCV: CoinAPI V1 primary, Binance REST fallback; quote/BBO: CoinAPI DS primary, Binance bookTicker fallback; funding/mark/premium-index: Binance WS or REST exclusive; OI: Binance REST primary, CoinAnk fallback; liquidations covered by a separate worker; orderbook depth: Binance REST+WS). (6) The worker must write only V2-namespaced data plane (suggested prefix v2:market:*) and a public status payload. (7) Tests must cover preserved legacy behavior + V2 safety upgrades (no real exchange mutating method invoked, no old Redis write contract). Trigger codex_review_v2_market_ingestor_from_legacy_baseline on emit.\n\nSYMBOL_UNIVERSE_CONTRACT_REQUIRED. Every V2 worker must read active symbol scope from