  `write_event_to_redis` discards the boolean returned by `write_event_to_stream`, but callers (`consume_events` and `run_wss_session`) treat `all(result.values())` as the write-success condition. If Redis hash writes succeed while `xadd` to `v2:liquidations:events` fails, events are counted as written and no `redis_write_failures` are raised, while downstream `v2/liquidation_levels_engine` misses the event stream payload.
